From: WL2GO
Subject: Add --hostbind to restrict the host interface to one address

Upstream binds the TCP command and data ports with INADDR_ANY and offers no
way to change it, so ardopcf's TNC control interface -- including transmit --
is reachable by anyone who can reach the machine. WL2GO always spawns ardopcf
locally, so it passes 127.0.0.1.

The upstream default is preserved: with no --hostbind, behaviour is unchanged.

KNOWN GAP -- CLOSED by patch 0006: lib/ws_server/ws_server.c binds
independently of this option, via its own getaddrinfo/bind, so enabling the
WebGUI would have brought a listener up on all interfaces and this file's
loopback guarantee would no longer have held on its own. Patch 0006 extends
--hostbind to that listener as well.

diff --git a/src/common/ARDOPC.c b/src/common/ARDOPC.c
index dc69a06..be39a2e 100644
--- a/src/common/ARDOPC.c
+++ b/src/common/ARDOPC.c
@@ -110,6 +110,9 @@ int Squelch = 5;
 int BusyDet = 5;
 enum _ARQBandwidth ARQBandwidth = B2000MAX;
 char HostPort[80] = "";
+// Address the host command/data listeners bind to. Empty means INADDR_ANY,
+// which is the historical behaviour. Set with --hostbind.
+char HostBindAddr[64] = "";
 int port = 8515;
 BOOL RadioControl = FALSE;
 BOOL SlowCPU = FALSE;
diff --git a/src/common/ARDOPCommon.c b/src/common/ARDOPCommon.c
index 518d8b6..b3bbec3 100644
--- a/src/common/ARDOPCommon.c
